llm_answer:
According to Context 1 (id=959), Medicare defines chronic low back pain (cLBP) as follows:

- Lasting 12 weeks or longer;
- Nonspecific, in that it has no identifiable systemic cause (i.e., not associated with metastatic, inflammatory, infectious, etc. disease);
- Not associated with surgery;
- Not associated with pregnancy.

Additionally, Medicare covers up to 20 acupuncture treatments annually, with an additional 8 sessions covered if there is improvement, and treatment must be discontinued if the patient is not improving or regressing.
